      "text": "Three years earlier than 2022, accounting for the fact that January has exactly 31 days\", \"February has a variable number of 28 days and 30 days, March has exactly 31 days,\" \"April has exactly 30 days, May has exactly 31 days, June has 30 days, July has exactly 31 days, August has 31 days, September has 30 days, October has exactly 31 days and December has 28 days, a total of 365 days, we get 1 year has 365 days. Therefore, three years ago have 3 * 365 = 1095 days.)\n\nWe find the least common denominator:\n\n$\\frac{1}{f_1} + \\frac{1}{f_2} + \\frac{1}{f_3} + \\frac{1}{f_4} \\le 1/f_1 + 1/f_2 + 1/f_3 + 1/f_4 = \\frac 13+\\frac 14+\\frac 16+\\frac 17 = \\frac{22}{42} = \\frac{11}{21}$\n\nAdd 1 to solve:\n\n$\\frac{11}{21} + 1 = \\frac{32}{21}$\n\nWe look for the model to multiply $\\frac{31}{31}$ with this fraction, so we find the least common denominator of 31:\n\n$\\frac{31}{31}( \\frac{11}{21} +1) = \\frac{321}{651}$\n\nThere are 365 days in total. (While 31 is the least common multiple of the 4 days of each student, 21 is the smallest common denominator. 651 is the smallest number that 42, 21, 31, and 365 all divide into.) $365 \\div 651 = \\boxed{5}$\n\nThis problem tests basic knowledge of mathematics in order to solve it, and there is some thinking required.\nFrom today, we calculate each student's working frequency and record the students' frequencies. Then look at the frequency to find the least common multiple and calculate until the answer.\nFrom the problem, we have the frequencies of the four people, and it is required to find the least common multiple and calculate until the answer is found.\nThus, the answer is $\\boxed{ \\mathbf \\text{5} }$",
