      "text": "We need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of 3, 4, 6, and 7 to determine when Darren, Wanda, Beatrice, and Chi will next be working together.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of each number:\n- 3 = 3\n- 4 = 2^2\n- 6 = 2 * 3\n- 7 = 7\n\nNext, we take the highest exponent for each prime number:\n- For the prime number 3, the highest exponent is 1 (twice in 4 or 6).\n- For the prime number 2, the highest exponent is 2 (once in 4).\n- For the prime number 7, the highest exponent is 1 (only in 7).\n\nMultiplying these prime factorizations gives us the LCM:\nLCM = 2^2 * 3 * 7 = 4 * 3 * 7 = 36\n\nSince Adam needs 36 study sessions to catch up at the rate of 2 sessions per session, we can solve for the number of sessions needed to catch up with 2 sessions per session for 36 nights: 36 / 2 = 18 sessions.\n\nThus, we need 4 days (14 sessions for 6 nights) to get 2 sessions, and 4 days ( 2 **** sessions for 7 nights) to get 2 sessions. Adding 14 + 2 **** + 2 days gives us a total of 18 days. \n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{18}",
